        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-hsk4-causes-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Premise or cause?",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Use the accepted-premise frame to draw a practical conclusion. The causal frame explains why an outcome occurs. Both need a real connection between the clauses.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "既然你喜欢，就买吧。",
                "pinyin": "jìrán nǐ xǐhuan ， jiù mǎi ba 。",
                "meaning": "Since you like it, go ahead and buy it.",
                "audio": "5d99e1026084ec7489f302dc39e032b15d277bd720e26143f2374f068bd7b07c"
              },
              {
                "text": "由于下雨，因此我们没有出去。",
                "pinyin": "yóuyú xiàyǔ ， yīncǐ wǒmen méiyǒu chūqù 。",
                "meaning": "Because it rained, we did not go out.",
                "audio": "7cd9ddc23503466e5f3508987c6d25ab5eced9e105d27d64e1463d1f88bcc32c"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
